","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Ukct5H3Wt6kJi9YIbbWc5","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"ZachSchiada70","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-05-25T20:13:39.000Z","updated_at":"2022-05-26T00:13:49.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Ukct5H3Wt6kJi9YIbbWc5","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Ukct5H3Wt6kJi9YIbbWc5"}},{"id":"mRGMS36jIIAaxb31jwdo3","ext":"jpg","post_id":"mRGMS36jIIAaxb31jwdo3","description":"","caption":"State forest bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":"State forest bridge","author":"ZachSchiada70","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-05-25T20:14:55.000Z","updated_at":"2022-05-26T00:15:56.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/mRGMS36jIIAaxb31jwdo3","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/mRGMS36jIIAaxb31jwdo3"}},{"id":"JAvnmb4EJo8fYxYmX59FA","ext":"jpg","post_id":"JAvnmb4EJo8fYxYmX59FA","description":"Add a Caption","caption":"below Moores Mill bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":"below Moores Mill bridge","author":"ZachSchiada70","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2022-05-25T20:06:50.000Z","updated_at":"2022-05-26T00:08:24.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/JAvnmb4EJo8fYxYmX59FA","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/JAvnmb4EJo8fYxYmX59FA"}},{"id":"NyLigAuNsSntmvwmtzW1r","ext":"jpg","post_id":"yZSPko0LT35RoYQhTpG7a","description":"This drop was fun to run at lower water. At the level of this picture, it was fun current to play in. This is about half a mile river left before Red Mountain Rd. Right at Red Mountain Road was the site of Bowling Mill and has a small rapid just before the bridge.","caption":"Deep Creek Drop","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-01-13T12:42:59.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:43:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/NyLigAuNsSntmvwmtzW1r","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/NyLigAuNsSntmvwmtzW1r"}},{"id":"ESx2u0KazcNXxWls6t7MX","ext":"jpg","post_id":"yZSPko0LT35RoYQhTpG7a","description":"River left is actually private property. It was not posted when we ran it, but be respectful if you are scouting or portaging here. River right is an option too, but it would be more difficult to portage or scout from that side. Current at this level was very strong starting about 100 ft before the drop, so scouting ahead of time is probably a good idea.","caption":"Moore's Mill Dam (From Below)","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-01-13T12:43:00.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:43:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/ESx2u0KazcNXxWls6t7MX","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/ESx2u0KazcNXxWls6t7MX"}},{"id":"4KOszEpqrvKRaMcCXrW85","ext":"jpg","post_id":"yZSPko0LT35RoYQhTpG7a","description":"","caption":"Moore's Mill Dam (From Above)","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-01-13T12:43:00.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:43:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/4KOszEpqrvKRaMcCXrW85","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/4KOszEpqrvKRaMcCXrW85"}},{"id":"BphYJOjXZgp0MOdUpE5oc","ext":"jpg","post_id":"yZSPko0LT35RoYQhTpG7a","description":"Not a very big rapid, but fun surfing. According to Paddling Eastern North Carolina by Paul Ferguson, this used to be the put in. It is private property on the banks here, so one cannot put in here anymore.","caption":"Harris Mill Ledge","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Zach Schiada","poi_id":"ZhxFUREJYuCgKFEUxObg5","photo_date":"2024-01-13T12:43:00.000Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T12:43:00.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/BphYJOjXZgp0MOdUpE5oc","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/BphYJOjXZgp0MOdUpE5oc"}},{"id":"882836","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885512","description":"","caption":"Upper Flat Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882836","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882836"}},{"id":"882835","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"885511","description":"","caption":"Upper Flat Dam","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/882835","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/882835"}}],"detail":{"id":"1072","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Data from Joe Greiner, local ex\n\nThis section of the Flat is probably less popular than the lower, which goes to Lake Michie but it is decent and on par with other similarly rated rivers around. However, unlike the section further downstream, there is no permit required for parking if you take out earlier than the suggested one. There is some limited parking on Red Mountain Rd. Another option that gets the best stuff and shortens the trip a bit is to park on the shoulder of Moore's Mill Rd, but make sure you stay on the Durham County side before the No Parking Signs start at the line for Person County. This avoids two miles of flat water for this section and the parking fee at State Forest Rd, which is either $60/year or $13/day for a day pass, which can be purchased [here](https://app.outdooraccess.com/#/listing/16084) if preferred.\n\nAt 3.35 miles from the South Flat put in, there is Moore's Mill busted dam. It can be run at low water and is probably worth portaging at higher levels. Scouting is recommended regardless, getting out well ahead of the drop since current is strong at higher levels. After the dam, there are two ledges before Moore's Mill Rd and one similar and slightly tricky ledge immediately after the bridge. I would love to know the names of these if they ever had them if anyone knows. ZCS","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"8.4","correlations":[{"reachID":"1072","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":"Very Scrapey","lowRunnableRangeComment":"Decent Low, Some Scraping","mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":"Consider portaging Moore's Mill Dam","aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":"IIstandoutIII","highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":"IItoIII","beginLowRunnable":"160","beginMediumRunnable":"400","beginHighRunnable":"900","endHighRunnable":"5000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"FLAT RIVER AT BAHAMA, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02085500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"40","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.45","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.18277778","longitude":"-78.87888889"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/02085500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02085500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"40","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["110161","ZhxFUREJYuCgKFEUxObg5","cj7EczxZ85KeKocC3O5sf","ZP47cDxXtrG6z0uGU74Pp","lI8Z5ovqoeYmqcLgqeMV1","115424"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-78.944645,36.256879],[-78.944449,36.25685],[-78.94392,36.256644],[-78.943337,36.255993],[-78.943003,36.255858],[-78.941779,36.255677],[-78.941001,36.255271],[-78.940612,36.254955],[-78.940222,36.25446],[-78.940001,36.253468],[-78.939556,36.253062],[-78.939179,36.2528